#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# log_log_plot

#% text
# `log_log_plot(f, [x, a, b])` plots `f` with logarithmic x and y axes, for `0 < a < b`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Power laws appear as straight lines; the slope is the exponent.

#% item
# It takes the options of `plot`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
log_log_plot([x^2, x^3], [x, 1, 100], legend: [r"$x^2$", r"$x^3$"])
#% output
#= image("log_log_plot.files/log_log_plot-1.svgz")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A spectrum over many decades:

#% cell
log_log_plot(x^3/(exp(x) - 1), [x, 0.01, 30], x_label: r"$x$")
#% output
#= image("log_log_plot.files/log_log_plot-2.svgz")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `plot`, `log_linear_plot`, `list_log_log_plot`
